# Database efficiency (Terrana ERP)

PostgreSQL/Supabase must stay fast as operational data grows.

## Schema & types

- Money (₦) and weights (kg): use **`NUMERIC`**, not `float`/`double precision`.
- Status, dates, foreign keys: add **indexes** on columns used in `WHERE`, `ORDER BY`, and joins.
- Prefer composite indexes for common filters, e.g. `(supplier_id, payment_status)`.

## Queries

- Every list endpoint/table view: **paginate** (default 25 rows).
- Use `count` with filters sparingly; prefer approximate counts or cached summaries on dashboards.
- Traceability chains (supplier → batch → shipment): load **full chain on detail pages only**, not list rows.

## RLS & security

- Keep policies simple — complex per-row logic slows every query.
- Use `security definer` functions only when necessary; index columns referenced in policies.

## Migrations

- Add indexes in the same migration as new tables when the access pattern is known.
- Never delete business records — use status changes; index `status` on high-volume tables.

## Dashboard (Phase 9)

- Pre-aggregate KPIs via **views or SQL functions**, not `COUNT(*)` across full tables on every page load.
